cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use PRISM-Q in published work, please cite it as below and name the release version used."
title: "PRISM-Q: quantum circuit simulator in Rust"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Coull
    given-names: A.
repository-code: "https://github.com/AbeCoull/prism-q"
url: "https://abecoull.github.io/prism-q/"
license:
  - MIT
  - Apache-2.0
abstract: >-
  PRISM-Q is an open-source quantum circuit simulator written in Rust with Python
  bindings. It reads OpenQASM 3.0, selects a simulation backend from the circuit's
  structure (statevector, stabilizer, sparse, matrix product state, product state,
  tensor network, density matrix, and factored variants), runs a multi-pass gate
  fusion pipeline, and executes on SIMD kernels, with optional CUDA acceleration and
  an optional MPI-distributed statevector.
keywords:
  - quantum computing
  - quantum circuit simulator
  - statevector simulation
  - stabilizer simulation
  - tensor network
  - OpenQASM
  - Rust
  - CUDA
  - MPI
